data.content:
Three things break. Here's each issue and the fix:

---

### 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — expression tree no longer compiles

EF Core 10 added a **non-expression `Func<>` overload** that now wins overload resolution, so your manually-built expression tree code won't compile. Replace the entire block with the much simpler imperative style:

```csharp
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

No more `Expression.Lambda` / `Expression.Call` needed.

---

### 2. Complex type columns — two breaking changes

**a) Duplicate names are now auto-uniquified.** `ShippingAddress.Street` and `BillingAddress.Street` previously shared one column; now they get `Street` and `Street1`. To keep the old schema, pin names explicitly:

```csharp
b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, p =>
    p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, p =>
    p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
```

**b) Nested complex types now use the full path.** `Order.Payment.BillingAddress.City` was `BillingAddress_City`; now it's `Payment_BillingAddress_City`. To preserve the old name:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>()
    .ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment)
    .ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress)
    .Property(a => a.City)
    .HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City");
```

Both of these will generate migrations that rename columns if you don't pin them.

---

### 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

Every method gained a `string logCommandText` parameter (for redacted SQL logging). Add it:

```csharp
public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
    IRelationalConnection connection,
    DbCommand command,
    DbContext context,
    Guid commandId,
    Guid connectionId,
    DateTimeOffset startTime,
    string logCommandText)   // ← new parameter
{
    // Use logCommandText for logging (may have constants redacted)
    // Use command.CommandText for actual executed SQL
}
```

Update **all** methods on the interface (`CommandReaderExecuted`, `CommandScalarExecuting`, etc.) the same way.
